BAR Droid phone version of BAR's Top Bar Buttons (luaui/widgets/gui_top_bar_buttons.lua): a press taken when the strip
of buttons is under the press itself, not when the pointer was over it at the last check. Its MousePress ends with
`if hoveringButtons then return true end`, worked out in Update from where the pointer was; a finger moves the pointer
and presses in one frame, so after the quit dialog was closed from the Quit button, the pointer left on the strip, the
next tap on the map was taken here and did nothing (dev phone upright, 2026-11-16;
docs/upstream/bar-topbar-buttons-press-hover.patch). The strip as BAR's own check has it: 31958's overStrip (only the
reveal band while auto-hidden buttons are away), the whole button area before it (test-31723, test-31836). Applied by
the engine (BarDroidPhoneLuaDir) to BAR's file as LuaUI loads it; if a block finds no place, BAR's own file runs.
The block ends at MousePress's own end: test-31992 put widget:AllowQuit between it and MouseWheel, which the block's
place once ran into (remake-check, 2026-11-18); that end alone is found once in 31958 and 31992 alike.

@@@ find
	if hoveringButtons then
		return true
	end
end
@@@ with
	-- BAR Droid (phone): the strip under the press itself, not under the pointer at the last check (a finger moves the
	-- pointer and presses in one frame: after the quit dialog closed from Quit, a tap on the map was taken here)
	if buttonsArea[1] then
		local bottom = (showButtons or not cfg.revealHeight) and buttonsArea[2]
			or (buttonsArea[4] - mathFloor(cfg.revealHeight * widgetScale))
		if mathIsInRect(x, y, buttonsArea[1], bottom, buttonsArea[3], buttonsArea[4]) then
			return true
		end
	end
end
@@@ end
